---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
// Headshot or intentional no-photo decision: [TODO] not yet confirmed by Austin.
// Building text-only for now rather than fabricating or sourcing a photo.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Austin Todd"
  description="Austin Todd is a UX designer and strategist based in the Dallas–Fort Worth area, working across UX strategy, accessibility governance, measurement, and organizational alignment."
>
  <section class="wrap about-hero">
    <div class="col-reading">
      <p class="about-hero__eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="about-hero__headline">
        I'm most useful when the problem matters but the path forward is not yet clear.
      </h1>
      <div class="about-hero__copy">
        <p>
          I'm Austin Todd, a UX designer and strategist based in the Dallas–Fort Worth area.
        </p>
        <p>
          I help teams make sense of complex problems: identifying what is actually preventing
          progress, bringing together the people who understand different parts of the system, and
          creating structures that move the work toward decisions.
        </p>
        <p>
          My professional background is in UX design and accessibility. I earned a BFA in
          Communication Design with a concentration in UX Design from the University of North
          Texas, then joined Mouser Electronics, where I progressed from UX Designer to UX
          Accessibility Designer II. I'm also an IAAP Certified Professional in Accessibility
          Core Competencies (CPACC).
        </p>
        <p>Accessibility became an unexpectedly broad strategic education.</p>
        <p>
          It required me to think about individual interfaces, but also about the organizational
          systems that determine whether accessible experiences are consistently delivered:
          standards, responsibilities, workflows, measurement, tooling, training, priorities, and
          governance.
        </p>
        <p>
          Over time, my role expanded from identifying accessibility issues to helping the
          organization answer larger questions:
        </p>
        <ul class="about-hero__list">
          <li>How should teams share responsibility for experience quality?</li>
          <li>How do we translate broad commitments into workable expectations?</li>
          <li>What evidence helps teams and leaders understand progress?</li>
          <li>How should UX demonstrate its contribution to product and business outcomes?</li>
          <li>How do we make decisions when no single person owns the complete answer?</li>
        </ul>
        <p>That is the work I want to continue doing.</p>
        <p>
          I'm not trying to leave accessibility behind. It remains an important part of how I
          understand quality, inclusion, and organizational responsibility. But I want to apply the
          strategic capabilities I developed through that work to a wider range of product and
          experience problems.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap contribute" aria-labelledby="contribute-heading">
    <h2 id="contribute-heading" class="contribute__heading">How I contribute</h2>
    <div class="contribute__grid">
      <div class="contribute__item">
        <h3>I notice structural problems</h3>
        <p>
          I often recognize when repeated confusion, manual effort, or stakeholder disagreement
          points to a missing system rather than an isolated execution issue.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="contribute__item">
        <h3>I make ambiguity discussable</h3>
        <p>
          I translate broad concerns into specific questions, decisions, and tradeoffs so people
          can respond to something concrete.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="contribute__item">
        <h3>I connect perspectives</h3>
        <p>
          I work across UX, research, development, QA, product, leadership, and subject-matter
          experts. I do not need everyone to begin with the same perspective, but I do need the
          process to make their reasoning visible.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="contribute__item">
        <h3>I leave behind structure</h3>
        <p>
          My work often results in frameworks, standards, reporting systems, decision tools, or
          governance models that help teams continue operating after the initial engagement.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap outside" aria-labelledby="outside-heading">
    <div class="col-reading">
      <h2 id="outside-heading" class="outside__heading">Outside work</h2>
      <p class="outside__copy">
        Outside UX, I'm interested in art museums, utilitarian ceramics, movies, plants, cooking,
        and spending time outdoors. I'm drawn to things that are thoughtfully made, quietly
        functional, and improved through attention to detail—which probably explains a lot about
        how I approach design too.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap looking-for" aria-labelledby="looking-for-heading">
    <div class="col-reading">
      <h2 id="looking-for-heading" class="looking-for__heading">What I'm looking for</h2>
      <div class="looking-for__copy">
        <p>
          I'm interested in UX Strategist, Experience Strategist, Design Strategist, Service
          Designer, and systems-oriented UX roles.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm especially interested in teams working on complex products or organizational
          problems where research, facilitation, measurement, and systems thinking are valued
          alongside design execution.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="looking-for__links">
        <a href="/">View my work</a>
        <a href="/resume">View resume</a>
        <a href="/contact">Contact me</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-5);
  }

  .about-hero__eyebrow {
    font-size: var(--step-meta);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-blue);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .about-hero__headline {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--step-case-title);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-hero__copy {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .about-hero__copy p {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .about-hero__list {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.4em;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .contribute {
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    border-top: var(--border-thin);
  }

  .contribute__heading {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--step-section);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .contribute__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .contribute__item h3 {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .contribute__item p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .outside,
  .looking-for {
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
    border-top: var(--border-thin);
  }

  .outside__heading,
  .looking-for__heading {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--step-section);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .outside__copy {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  .looking-for__copy {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .looking-for__links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .looking-for__links a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding-inline: var(--space-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-blue);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-blue);
  }

  .looking-for__links a:hover {
    background: var(--color-blue-field);
  }
</style>
